<?xml version="1.0" encoding="UTF-8"?>
<!DOCTYPE plist PUBLIC "-//Apple//DTD PLIST 1.0//EN" "http://www.apple.com/DTDs/PropertyList-1.0.dtd">
<plist version="1.0">
<dict>
	<!-- §3.7 / nfc_contact_exchange: contact exchange via NDEF tag-in-tag
	     writes (see `lib/core/contact/nfc_android.dart`, `Ndef.write`).
	     No FeliCa/ISO7816/ISO15693/MiFare use anywhere in `lib/` — NDEF is
	     the only format the app reads or writes, so it is the only one
	     requested here. Required by the `nfc_manager` plugin's own iOS
	     setup instructions (pub.dev, "Near Field Communication Tag Reader
	     Session Formats Entitlement"); without it, `NfcManager.instance
	     .startSession` fails at the OS level regardless of
	     NFCReaderUsageDescription (Info.plist:73), which only covers the
	     usage-description dialog, not the capability itself.

	     Requires the "Near Field Communication Tag Reading" capability to
	     be enabled for this App ID in the Apple Developer portal, and the
	     "Cleona Distribution" provisioning profile regenerated afterwards
	     — otherwise codesign fails ("profile doesn't support this
	     capability") on the very next Manual-signed build (CODE_SIGN_STYLE
	     = Manual, project.pbxproj). UNGEPRUEFT: no Apple device or Xcode
	     available in this session to confirm the profile already carries
	     it. -->
	<key>com.apple.developer.nfc.readersession.formats</key>
	<array>
		<string>NDEF</string>
	</array>

	<!-- §11 / `lib/core/tagline/lan_entry_wiring.dart:58`:
	     `rufSock.joinMulticast(InternetAddress(kLanEntryMulticastV4))` on
	     239.192.67.76 (`lan_entry.dart:276`), unconditional on every
	     platform including iOS — cross-subnet LAN peer discovery. Without
	     this entitlement, iOS refuses the join at the socket level; the
	     call already fails NAMED rather than silently
	     (`lan_entry_wiring.dart:58-64`: try/catch, logs "Multicast-Gruppe
	     nicht beigetreten" and falls back to broadcast-only), so a missing
	     or rejected grant degrades discovery to same-segment-only instead
	     of breaking anything — see the session report for detail.

	     RESTRICTED entitlement: requires an explicit request to Apple
	     (Developer portal, "Multicast Networking" additional capability),
	     which Apple can decline. Add regardless of outcome, per Beschluss
	     E-5: it either becomes true after approval, or the Xcode capability
	     toggle is turned back off and this key removed again — a single,
	     visible edit either way, not a silent gap. UNGEPRUEFT: no Apple
	     device or Xcode available in this session; Apple DTS staff has
	     stated this entitlement is not consulted on macOS (see the session
	     report), so it is NOT added to macos/Runner/*.entitlements. -->
	<key>com.apple.developer.networking.multicast</key>
	<true/>
</dict>
</plist>
